When working on the next feature branch that touches directory data:

1. Ensure that migration is included before `db:testing:push` / prod push.
2. Prefer adding import-script validation so new Excel batches do not reintroduce clinic brands.
3. Do **not** edit old INSERT migrations in place unless doing a full directory replace — the cleanup migration is the safe fix for historical inserts.

## Curated finder photos

None: cards use the uploaded avatar or the default gender avatar. The empty maps-link photo map (`lib/finder-manual-photos.ts`) was removed in Point E5. See `.cursor/rules/manual-directory-preserved-photos.mdc`.

## App code touchpoints (when schema or fields change)

| Area | File |
|------|------|
| Finder load + card data | `app/finder/[[...filters]]/page.tsx` |
| Disabled calendar + request overlay | `components/finder/FinderManualCardAvailabilityGrid.tsx`, `useManualBookingRequestFeedback.tsx` |
| Call to Book phone | `components/finder/FinderClinicLocationBlock.tsx`, `RevealPhoneButton.tsx` |
| Phone `tel:` links | `lib/phone-link.ts` |
| Patient vote API | `app/api/directory-manual/patient-booking-request/route.ts` |
| Sitemap pairs | `app/sitemap.ts` |
| Internal duplicate queue | `app/internal/directory/page.tsx` |

## Deploy workflow

1. Create/edit migration(s) in `supabase/migrations/`.
2. **Testing first:** `npm run db:testing:push` (project `fwinchqdgrkpxuuttech`).
3. Verify `/finder/{district}/{specialty}`, Call to Book phone, distance sort.
4. **Production only when user explicitly asks:** `npm run db:prod:push` — never assume prior consent.
5. Before prod directory changes, run test-profile preflight per `prod-directory-test-profile-safety.mdc`.

## Safety rules (always)

- Never push prod DB without explicit user request in the current task.
- Manual directory has no `is_test_profile` column, but still avoid junk/test names in curated data.
- Product copy in UI stays **English** (Greek only where product already supports it).
